                <pb facs="0852" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.119/1839: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-20T15:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 20, 1918—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3572. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]: No. 1894. Embassy’s 4613 December 14,
                    your 2093. Referring to the stipulation <pb facs="0853" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/>
                    concerning the discontinuance of X cables that no licenses will be granted here
                    to consignees on the Statlist or GBLA, we assume that the foregoing does not
                    apply to the “free list” for the Northern Neutrals with respect to which we
                    understand that the British propose to refuse licenses to only consignees on
                    Statlist.</p>
                <p>Embassy’s 4513 December 11, 3 p.m. your 2056. Department’s 3358 December 10, 3
                    p.m., our 1813 expresses the opinion of the War Trade Board. Our feeling is that
                    unity of action is the matter of fundamental importance and we feel that a
                    complete understanding of the purpose underlying the modifications proposed by
                    the British and the urgency of the British view in regard thereto is essential
                    to enable us to keep policies in substantial accord.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
